  "generated_text": "To solve the equation \\((z^2 - 3z + 1)^2 - 3(z^2 - 3z + 1) + 1 = z\\), we start by making a substitution. Let \\( w = z^2 - 3z + 1 \\). Then the equation becomes:\n\n\\[ w^2 - 3w + 1 = z. \\]\n\nWe also know that \\( w = z^2 - 3z + 1 \\). To find possible values of \\( w \\), we substitute \\( z = w \\) into the equation \\( w = z^2 - 3z + 1 \\):\n\n\\[ w = w^2 - 3w + 1. \\]\n\nRearranging terms, we get a quadratic equation in \\( w \\):\n\n\\[ w^2 - 4w + 1 = 0. \\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( w = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = -4 \\), and \\( c = 1 \\):\n\n\\[ w = \\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{16 - 4}}{2} = \\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{12}}{2} = \\frac{4 \\pm 2\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 2 \\pm \\sqrt{3}. \\]\n\nSo, the solutions for \\( w \\) are \\( w = 2 + \\sqrt{3} \\) and \\( w = 2 - \\sqrt{3} \\).\n\nNext, we substitute these values back into the equation \\( w^2 - 3w + 1 = z \\).\n\n1. For \\( w = 2 + \\sqrt{3} \\):\n\n\\[ z^2 - 3z + 1 = 2 + \\sqrt{3}. \\]\n\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\n\\[ z^2 - 3z + 1 - 2 - \\sqrt{3} = 0 \\]\n\\[ z^2 - 3z - 1 - \\sqrt{3} = 0. \\]\n\nThe solutions to this quadratic equation are:\n\n\\[ z = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{9 + 4(1 + \\sqrt{3})}}{2} = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{13 + 4\\sqrt{3}}}{2}. \\]\n\n2. For \\( w = 2 - \\sqrt{3} \\):\n\n\\[ z^2 - 3z + 1 = 2 - \\sqrt{3}. \\]\n\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\n\\[ z^2 - 3z + 1 - 2 + \\sqrt{3} = 0 \\]\n\\[ z^2 - 3z - 1 + \\sqrt{3} = 0. \\]\n\nThe solutions to this quadratic equation are:\n\n\\[ z = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{9 + 4(1 - \\sqrt{3})}}{2} = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{13 - 4\\sqrt{3}}}{2}. \\]\n\nThus, the solutions to the original equation are:\n\n\\[ z = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{13 + 4\\sqrt{3}}}{2}, \\quad z = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{13 + 4\\sqrt{3}}}{2}, \\quad z = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{13 - 4\\sqrt{3}}}{2}, \\quad z = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{13 - 4\\sqrt{3}}}{2}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the solutions are:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{13 + 4\\sqrt{3}}}{2}, \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{13 + 4\\sqrt{3}}}{2}, \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{13 - 4\\sqrt{3}}}{2}, \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{13 - 4\\sqrt{3}}}{2}}. \\]",
